@page "/"

<PageTitle>au-btech-literature-review-agent</PageTitle>

<header class="bg-[#003B5C] text-white flex-none shrink-0 z-50 shadow-md">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 h-14 flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
        <a href="/" class="flex items-center space-x-3 hover:opacity-90 transition-opacity min-w-0 shrink overflow-hidden">
            <span class="flex-none bg-white rounded-md p-0.5"><img src="img/logo.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" class="h-7 w-7" /></span>
            <span class="font-bold tracking-tight text-xs sm:text-sm whitespace-nowrap truncate">AARHUS UNIVERSITY</span>
            <span class="text-white/40 font-light hidden lg:inline">|</span>
            <span class="text-xs tracking-wider font-medium opacity-90 uppercase hidden lg:inline">au-btech-literature-review-agent</span>
        </a>
    </div>
</header>

<main class="flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto bg-white text-gray-900">

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="border-b border-gray-200">
        <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-12 lg:py-20 grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-10 lg:gap-14 items-center">
            <div>
            <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-[#003B5C] mb-5">
                Aarhus University &middot; Department of Business Development and Technology
            </p>
            <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl lg:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900 break-words">
                TraceableAI
            </h1>
            <p class="font-serif text-xl lg:text-2xl text-gray-700 mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-snug">
                Systematic literature reviews you can check afterwards.
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm lg:text-base text-gray-600 mt-6 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
                An open-source agent that runs PRISMA 2020&ndash;compliant literature reviews and keeps a
                record of every step, so every statement in the final report can be traced back to the paper
                it came from.
            </p>

            <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
                <a href="/review"
                   class="bg-[#003B5C] text-white px-7 py-3 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider hover:bg-[#00293f] transition-colors">
                    Get Started
                </a>
                <a href="https://github.com/lauPhilip/au-btech-literature-review-agent"
                   class="border border-gray-300 text-gray-800 px-7 py-3 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider hover:border-[#003B5C] hover:text-[#003B5C] transition-colors">
                    View on GitHub
                </a>
            </div>

            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-6">
                Try it with a few free runs a day, or add your own Mistral API key for more. Free and open
                source under the Apache 2.0 license.
            </p>
            </div>
            <figure class="order-first lg:order-none">
                <img src="img/campus-960.webp" srcset="img/campus-480.webp 480w, img/campus-960.webp 960w" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 520px, 100vw"
                     width="960" height="717" alt="Illustration: a friendly robot reads a tablet under a tree on a university campus while students walk by." fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"
                     class="w-full h-auto rounded-xl shadow-lg ring-1 ring-black/5" />
            </figure>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What it does -->
    <section class="border-b border-gray-200">
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
            <h2 class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-400 mb-8">What it does</h2>
            <figure class="mb-8">
                <img src="img/library-960.webp" srcset="img/library-480.webp 480w, img/library-960.webp 960w" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 1024px, 100vw"
                     width="960" height="717" alt="Illustration: a robot reads a large book in a university library while library drones fetch books from the shelves." loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                     class="w-full h-48 sm:h-64 lg:h-72 object-cover rounded-xl shadow-md ring-1 ring-black/5" />
            </figure>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-px bg-gray-200 border border-gray-200">
                <div class="bg-white p-7">
                    <h3 class="font-serif text-lg text-gray-900 mb-2">Protocol first</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                        The review question, criteria and sources are written down and
                        fingerprinted before any search runs. Any later change, such as the
                        extra search phrasings, is added as a dated amendment.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-white p-7">
                    <h3 class="font-serif text-lg text-gray-900 mb-2">Screened twice, disagreements flagged</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                        Every record is screened by two independent prompts. Where they
                        disagree, the paper is kept and flagged, and the agreement between the
                        two is reported as Cohen&rsquo;s kappa. The least certain decisions are
                        shown to you first.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-white p-7">
                    <h3 class="font-serif text-lg text-gray-900 mb-2">Every citation checked against the paper</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                        Each cited sentence is compared with the text of the paper it cites, and
                        the verdict comes with a verbatim quote. The tool checks that the quote
                        really is in the paper, so an unsupported claim is flagged instead of
                        trusted.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-white p-7">
                    <h3 class="font-serif text-lg text-gray-900 mb-2">Data extraction and quality appraisal</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                        For each included study it extracts the method, sample, findings and
                        limitations, and appraises quality with MMAT 2018. Every value is backed
                        by a quote that is checked against the source.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-white p-7">
                    <h3 class="font-serif text-lg text-gray-900 mb-2">Open sources and citation chaining</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                        It searches arXiv, OpenAlex, Semantic Scholar and Crossref out of the
                        box, and follows the references and citing papers of the included
                        studies to find work the search missed.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="bg-white p-7">
                    <h3 class="font-serif text-lg text-gray-900 mb-2">A complete, verifiable record</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                        Every run produces one archive: the protocol, the raw source responses,
                        every screening decision, every model call, the citation audit, a draft
                        manuscript in LaTeX, BibTeX and RIS files, and a manifest that
                        fingerprints every file.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- How it works -->
    <section class="border-b border-gray-200">
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
            <h2 class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-400 mb-8">How it works</h2>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-5 gap-10 items-start">
            <ol class="space-y-6 lg:col-span-3">
                <li class="flex gap-5">
                    <span class="flex-none w-8 h-8 bg-[#003B5C] text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold">1</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="font-serif text-lg text-gray-900">Write the protocol</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1">
                            You give the question, the inclusion and exclusion criteria and the
                            sources. The tool saves them as the review protocol before it
                            searches.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li class="flex gap-5">
                    <span class="flex-none w-8 h-8 bg-[#003B5C] text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold">2</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="font-serif text-lg text-gray-900">Search</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1">
                            It queries arXiv, OpenAlex, Semantic Scholar and Crossref (plus
                            Scopus and IEEE Xplore when a key is set) with your query and a few
                            extra phrasings, keeps the raw response of every query, and removes
                            duplicates.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li class="flex gap-5">
                    <span class="flex-none w-8 h-8 bg-[#003B5C] text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold">3</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="font-serif text-lg text-gray-900">Screen</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1">
                            Each record is screened twice against your criteria. If you like,
                            the run pauses so you can include or exclude papers yourself,
                            starting with the uncertain ones; your decisions are recorded.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li class="flex gap-5">
                    <span class="flex-none w-8 h-8 bg-[#003B5C] text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold">4</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="font-serif text-lg text-gray-900">Follow the citations</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1">
                            The references and citing papers of the included studies are fetched
                            through OpenAlex and screened the same way.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li class="flex gap-5">
                    <span class="flex-none w-8 h-8 bg-[#003B5C] text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold">5</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="font-serif text-lg text-gray-900">Read and appraise</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1">
                            Open-access full text is fetched where it legally exists; otherwise
                            the abstract is used. Each study is extracted and appraised with
                            MMAT, and every quote is checked.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li class="flex gap-5">
                    <span class="flex-none w-8 h-8 bg-[#003B5C] text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold">6</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="font-serif text-lg text-gray-900">Write and check the report</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1">
                            The evidence is mapped to themes before any prose is written. The
                            synthesis cites the studies, and every cited sentence is then
                            checked against the paper it cites.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li class="flex gap-5">
                    <span class="flex-none w-8 h-8 bg-[#003B5C] text-white flex items-center justify-center text-sm font-bold">7</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3 class="font-serif text-lg text-gray-900">Download the record</h3>
                        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mt-1">
                            You get the PRISMA report with clickable citations, a PRISMA flow
                            diagram, and the full run archive to share, archive or check later.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </li>
            </ol>
            <figure class="lg:col-span-2 lg:sticky lg:top-6">
                <img src="img/lab-960.webp" srcset="img/lab-480.webp 480w, img/lab-960.webp 960w" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 400px, 100vw"
                     width="960" height="717" alt="Illustration: a robot examines a circuit board under a microscope in a laboratory while researchers work at their benches." loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                     class="w-full h-auto rounded-xl shadow-md ring-1 ring-black/5" />
                <figcaption class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-3 leading-relaxed">Every step leaves a record you can check: the protocol, the raw search results, each screening decision and each citation verdict.</figcaption>
            </figure>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Why traceability -->
    <section class="border-b border-gray-200">
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
            <h2 class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-400 mb-8">Why traceability</h2>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-10 items-center">
            <div class="border-l-2 border-[#003B5C] pl-6">
                <p class="font-serif text-lg lg:text-xl text-gray-800 leading-relaxed">
                    Automated review tools tend to produce fluent text with citations that are broken or
                    invented. That makes them hard to trust, and unsuitable for standards like PRISMA 2020,
                    where you are expected to show how you reached your conclusions. This agent does not ask
                    to be trusted: it keeps the whole trail, checks its own citations, and tells you where it
                    is unsure, so a person can verify the review and stay responsible for it.
                </p>
            </div>
            <figure>
                <img src="img/classroom-960.webp" srcset="img/classroom-480.webp 480w, img/classroom-960.webp 960w" sizes="(min-width: 768px) 480px, 100vw"
                     width="960" height="717" alt="Illustration: a robot teacher explains a diagram at a blackboard to a class of robot students." loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                     class="w-full h-auto rounded-xl shadow-md ring-1 ring-black/5" />
            </figure>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Footer -->
    <footer>
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-10 flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-center md:justify-between gap-4">
